# db-backup Licensing

db-backup is distributed under a layered licensing model. Different parts of the tree (and the container image) carry different licenses, so which license
applies depends on which part you use:

| Layer               | What it covers                                                                     | License             |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| Core software       | `internal/`, `cmd/` — the Community edition of the `dbb` binary                    | AGPL-3.0-or-later   |
| Supported features  | `supported/` — compiled into the full `dbb` binary                                 | NSLv1 (proprietary) |
| Container packaging | `container/` — the `Containerfile`, `container/rootfs/*` scripts and configuration | MIT                 |

## Community edition (AGPL-3.0-or-later)

The entire codebase outside the `supported/` directory is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later.

- Full license text: [`LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt`](LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt)
- You can build the pure Community binary with: `make build-community`

## Supported edition (NSLv1 — proprietary)

The code under the `supported/` directory is licensed under the Nfrastack Supporter License v1 (NSLv1), a proprietary commercial license.
You may view and compile this code, but running the Supported features in production requires a valid, active license key issued by Nfrastack.

- Full license text: [`LICENSES/LicenseRef-NSLv1.txt`](LICENSES/LicenseRef-NSLv1.txt) and [`supported/LICENSE.md`](supported/LICENSE.md)
- The default build (`make build`) produces the full binary with the Supported features compiled in. A key unlocks it at runtime.

## Container image (MIT packaging)

The container image itself is licensed under the MIT License. See [`container/LICENSE`](container/LICENSE).

The `dbb` binary bundled in the image is MIT-licensed; it is built from the AGPL core plus the NSLv1 `supported/` tree (full build), or from the
AGPL core alone (community build). See the sections above for those licenses.

